WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.440
Bad information impacts all of us.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.440
Scams threaten all of our finances.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.440
Political misinformation undermines
our democracy.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.440
When it comes to the
coronavirus pandemic,

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.640
health misinformation threatens
all of our lives.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.440
In human history, it has never been
so easy to spread misinformation

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.040
to millions of people so rapidly.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.200
My name is Laura Walters,
I'm a journalist,

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.440
and I have been a victim
of misinformation.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:51.400
I got a cold call from a new website
looking to publish news content.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.000
Everything seemed very normal,
like any other freelance commission.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.280
I wrote the story on Chinese
influence in New Zealand,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.680
and then I literally thought nothing
more of it.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.320
And about three or four
months later, I got a call.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.480
Turns out that the FBI had actually
tipped off Facebook.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.040
This news organisation wasn't
a news organisation at all.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.520
It was the same troll farm

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.520
that meddled in the 2016
US presidential elections.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.600
From there it's been a deep
dive into learning about

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.680
how our networks are infiltrated
to try and spread misinformation.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.320
I could have completely
avoided this situation

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.000
if I had applied the scrutiny
in the same way that I do

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.520
when I'm investigating
a story myself.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.440
If I can show how it happened to me,

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.640
maybe I can help other
people avoid it.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.520
It's been a real wild
experience for me.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.520
It's important to remind people

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.880
of the dangers of information

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:56.880
and the new ways

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.240
that people can share information

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.640
that present risks to all of us,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.640
but also the internet as a means
of sharing good information.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.120
Yes, we're all confronted with
more information than ever

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.080
which makes it hard to tell
fact from fiction,

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.920
but at the same time,
fact-checkers like us

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.240
can use the internet and the reach
that we have to correct the record

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.200
quicker than we ever could,
and directly to people.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:25.840
You can verify a story in many cases

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.200
by simply typing in

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.600
the claim that you're
not very sure of

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.240
and putting "fact check" next to it,
for example,

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.160
on your preferred search engine.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.000
There's a very good chance
that the top result

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:43.000
will actually take you to one of the
fact checking organisations' website

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.400
that has already looked into
that claim.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.760
Fact checking organisations have
looked into well over 100,000 claims

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.720
just when the pandemic started.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.400
Within one year, they have looked
at over 10,000 claims

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.280
only related to the pandemic.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.600
There were quite a few
stories circulating

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.760
that were false, that were offering
very simple cures to the disease,

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.880
such as if you inhale steam.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.680
-And that it would cure coronavirus
just seemed completely illogical.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.680
But when people are just overwhelmed
by the amount of information

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.600
and they're scared
and they're anxious,

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.080
it shows that they
can believe things.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.960
It's interesting, when
we're sort of anxious

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.840
we have, on the one hand, a need to
actively go out and find information

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.640
as a way of explaining what's going
on, or even to help keep us safe.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.760
But at the same time,
the research shows

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.680
we also experience paradoxical
inability to process complexity,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.280
which, all together, means
that when we are anxious

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.160
we are even more susceptible
to bad information.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.400
There are tools online to verify,
for example, fake images.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.800
One of them is Google
reverse image search

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.440
where you put in an image
and search for that image.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.520
It is a really useful way

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.440
of seeing where that image
originally came from.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.960
Something like this would be
a huge news story

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:28.480
so if it's not being reported
by trusted news sources

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.640
that might be a clue
that it's not actually true.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.080
Deepfakes is a big concern,

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.400
and it's a growing concern, because
it's completely new technology.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.000
The wonderful world of deepfakes.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.520
AI and VFX.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.360
In the future that technology's
going to be perfected

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.880
and then we would really struggle

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.960
to tell whether that video
is not what it's meant to be.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.200
And so more technology is coming out

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.200
that would help curb the spread
of misinformation

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.880
in the form of plug-ins
or that you could download

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.120
and attach to your browser.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.520
They could tell you what's less
credible and what's more credible.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.840
Algorithms that could help the
social media platforms

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.600
to detect automatically
and very rapidly

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.720
which stories being circulated
that are not true.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.880
I'm quite hopeful on our ability

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.120
to tackle the spread
of misinformation in the future

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.960
because more people are aware
of the issue

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:32.360
because AI technology is becoming
far more effective and powerful

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.400
in determining what is credible
and what isn't

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.640
and then reducing, if not stopping
the spread, of that misinformation.

